00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:29.520
And we're going to have our last
cool thing of the week, which

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:32.516
is something that, in my
opinion, is super cool.

00:06:32.516 --> 00:06:34.890
I don't know if you've ever
heard about this thing called

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:35.900
Quick, Draw!

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:36.860
Quick, Draw!

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:38.190
with Google.com.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:41.100
And it's this little app that
you can use on your phone

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:45.285
or on your computer, and
basically you access it

00:06:45.285 --> 00:06:48.430
and you draw whatever,
and it guesses what it is.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:50.520
So it's kind of like Pictionary.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:53.280
And this is powered by
machine learning, of course,

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.790
with neural networks and
convolutional neural networks.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.880
The cool thing is that
convolutional networks

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:02.790
are cool, but they
need a lot of data.

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:04.620
And we just open
sourced that data,

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.830
the data that was used to train
that neural network, which

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:09.420
is super useful
because then you can

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:10.770
do whatever you want with that.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:14.340
You can train how to
do Pictionary again,

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.650
but also you can
do more analysis.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:20.910
Like, according to all of
these drawings of a cat,

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:23.840
what does a cat look like
according to each country?

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:26.670
And you can do an average
and be like, cats in Japan

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.220
are actually slightly different
to cats in the United States.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.100
It is really cool.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:33.060
You can do lots of really
cool data processing.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:38.460
And also, the data even includes
not only the finished drawing

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:41.160
but also how it was
drawn, so you can actually

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.510
follow the traces.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:44.940
