MELANIE WARRICK:
But you've got time.

00:32:56.080 --> 00:32:56.570
MARK MANDEL: I've got time.

00:32:56.570 --> 00:32:58.320
MELANIE WARRICK: You've
got plenty of time

00:32:58.320 --> 00:33:01.120
FRANCESC CAMPOY: So there was
there was this clash of titans.

00:33:01.120 --> 00:33:05.440
There was Mark
Zuckerberg and Elon Musk

00:33:05.440 --> 00:33:07.660
publicly discussing AI.

00:33:07.660 --> 00:33:10.810
And basically, one is saying
AI is super dangerous,

00:33:10.810 --> 00:33:12.740
we should be super
careful with it.

00:33:12.740 --> 00:33:15.710
The other one was like,
no, AI will save the world.

00:33:15.710 --> 00:33:17.500
What is your bent on this?

00:33:17.500 --> 00:33:19.870
What is your opinion?

00:33:19.870 --> 00:33:22.150
Will AI destroy
or save the world?

00:33:22.150 --> 00:33:23.230
MARK MANDEL: And it can
only be one or the other.

00:33:23.230 --> 00:33:23.890
There's no in between.

00:33:23.890 --> 00:33:24.910
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:33:24.910 --> 00:33:28.180
MELANIE WARRICK:
I plead the fifth.

00:33:28.180 --> 00:33:31.634
So I've seen this argument
playing out, especially

00:33:31.634 --> 00:33:32.800
in the last couple of years.

00:33:32.800 --> 00:33:35.770
I think that the fear
is used to get people

00:33:35.770 --> 00:33:37.960
to do things or
to, I don't know,

00:33:37.960 --> 00:33:40.000
react in ways that
is not necessarily

00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:42.400
as beneficial, frankly.

00:33:42.400 --> 00:33:45.010
I'm not a fan of doing a lot
of, let's be afraid, let's

00:33:45.010 --> 00:33:46.210
be really afraid.

00:33:46.210 --> 00:33:49.460
But I do think you
need to be careful.

00:33:49.460 --> 00:33:51.100
And I know a lot
of the researchers

00:33:51.100 --> 00:33:54.730
are trying to advocate
for some of the challenges

00:33:54.730 --> 00:33:57.940
that they see coming
and trying to advocate

00:33:57.940 --> 00:34:02.197
responsibly for ways we can come
up against those challenges.

00:34:02.197 --> 00:34:04.030
I know this isn't as
much fun as, yeah, they

00:34:04.030 --> 00:34:06.980
should throw down
and fight it out,

00:34:06.980 --> 00:34:09.400
and this is the best
person in there.

00:34:09.400 --> 00:34:11.485
I do see there's a lot
of hype in this space.

00:34:11.485 --> 00:34:14.650
There's a lot of hype, and
it is concerning in some ways

00:34:14.650 --> 00:34:16.630
because I think people
can get caught up in it

00:34:16.630 --> 00:34:19.870
and make poor decisions
and buy into things

00:34:19.870 --> 00:34:22.480
that are not going to be useful
for them in the long run.

00:34:22.480 --> 00:34:25.989
But, unlike the
past with AI, where

00:34:25.989 --> 00:34:30.600
we saw hype in the '50s and
then this AI winter and hype

00:34:30.600 --> 00:34:33.880
again in like the '80s and
'90s and again a dropout,

00:34:33.880 --> 00:34:38.560
we are seeing real applications,
like identifying cancer cells

00:34:38.560 --> 00:34:42.480
in images, that are beneficial,
so beneficial to us.

00:34:42.480 --> 00:34:46.750
And so this isn't completely
overhyped in terms of there's

00:34:46.750 --> 00:34:47.989
not some real value there.

00:34:47.989 --> 00:34:52.090
It's just you have to be careful
about the hype and the fear

00:34:52.090 --> 00:34:55.330
and be realistic about
what is it being used for,

00:34:55.330 --> 00:34:59.950
where is it useful, and
then see what you need to do

00:34:59.950 --> 00:35:01.422
to be responsible about it.

00:35:01.422 --> 00:35:03.380
FRANCESC CAMPOY: You
