00:35:37.730 --> 00:35:39.840
but there are some
conversations and discussion

00:35:39.840 --> 00:35:41.750
of what does that look like.

00:35:41.750 --> 00:35:44.660
Some other concerns are along
what you were talking about

00:35:44.660 --> 00:35:46.880
before, with testing,
and how do we

00:35:46.880 --> 00:35:49.070
know we're putting stuff
out into the wild that

00:35:49.070 --> 00:35:50.630
is not going to harm people?

00:35:50.630 --> 00:35:52.760
And make sure we
have the right level.

00:35:52.760 --> 00:35:53.450
And I say harm.

00:35:53.450 --> 00:35:55.950
I'm not talking about them
killing everybody off,

00:35:55.950 --> 00:35:59.420
but I am saying having the
right safeguards in place.

00:35:59.420 --> 00:36:03.422
So they're not completely off
base those who talk about this,

00:36:03.422 --> 00:36:05.630
and I know [? Yomas ?] is
one of those, where they're

00:36:05.630 --> 00:36:08.690
trying to say, do we
have the right safeguards

00:36:08.690 --> 00:36:11.867
to make sure that AI is going
to be impactful in useful ways?

00:36:11.867 --> 00:36:14.450
MARK MANDEL: And like what you
